WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.620
What happened up there?

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.390
I was pushed out. By Ruri.

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.590
What?

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.520
Your sister has changed...

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:15.910
That's impossible.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.530
Ruri!

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.430
Wait! It's dangerous!

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.720
Something might be controlling her!

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.900
Controlling?

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.110
Yes... I've heard that the Professor has

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.310
a duelist that can control people's minds.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.220
If Ruri's being controlled...

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.730
Then, in the eastern tower, as well...

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.720
Edo...

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.970
A man named Hugo headed 
for the eastern tower.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.310
You tell Hugo the truth.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:47.480
I'll go after Syun!

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.760
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.530
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:59.340
Their dragons call to each other,

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:02.590
almost as if seeking one another.

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:41.010
The Songbird Fallen Into Darkness

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:44.580
Ruri!

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.180
Wait, Syun!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.650
Ruri!

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.620
Brother?

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:51.610
Ruri!

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.550
Brother!

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.310
Finally... I've finally found you.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.260
I've wanted to see you...

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.770
Hey, Kaito...

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.120
He came to save me, but the next 
thing I knew, he was gone.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.830
I'm right here.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.440
Ruri, you don't remember 
what you did to me?

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:14.910
Enough. Don't say any more.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.050
Edo explained it to you.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:21.580
The Professor has a duelist 
that can control people.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.920
That duelist is probably controlling Ruri!

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.400
I'm being controlled?

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.360
What are you talking about? 
What are you saying?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.620
Listen to me, Kaito...

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.000
You must have made a mistake.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.520
The Ruri standing here is clearly my 
real little sister, Ruri Kurosaki!

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:41.050
Nothing is different about her.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.620
She's the normal Ruri.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.050
I'm her big brother, so I 
can say that for sure!

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:52.580
It is always amusing to watch 
allies argue with each other.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.470
But I'm afraid things must proceed...

00:03:55.470 --> 00:04:01.050
Now, will the bond between siblings 
overcome the Professor's will?

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.460
Let's test it and see.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.120
Ruri!

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.270
L-Let me go!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.860
You must see it now, Syun.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.520
Ruri isn't in her right mind.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.210
How dare you do this to Ruri?

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.460
Academia, you will pay.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.680
I will make you pay!

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.380
Now, let's duel!

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:36.960
Syun, I'll search for the one controlling Ruri.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.090
You handle things here!

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:05.590
Another Academia student, 
turned into a card...

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.930
Just who is doing this?

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.770
It's dangerous to stay separated.

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:12.160
We'd better find Sawatari 
and Crow right away!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.260
Yeah.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.120
Where are you, Sawatari?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.730
Sawatari! Hey!

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.810
Who is it that's been following me?

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.290
Field Spell Crossover.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.380
Duel!

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.840
I'll take the first move.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.140
I summon Raidraptor — Vanishing 
Lanius from my hand.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.720
When I succeed in summoning it,

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.720
I can Special Summon another 
Vanishing Lanius from my hand.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.630
This Retrofit Lanius can be 
treated as identical to another

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.690
Raidraptor monster on my side of the field.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:25.020
Thus, I Special Summon Retrofit 
Lanius as a Vanishing Lanius!

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:35.110
And one Retrofit Lanius can count as two 
components for an Xyz Summon.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:41.050
I overlay the Level 4 Vanishing 
Lanius and Retrofit Lanius.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:47.620
Hidden falcon, raise your sharpened 
claws from adversity

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.560
and show your wings of rebellion!

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:52.780
Xyz Summon!

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:57.900
Appear, Rank 4 Raidraptor — Rise Falcon!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.860
Ruri, you could once do nothing, 
without me by your side...

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.140
For you to turn you fangs against me...

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.910
I set one card and end my turn.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:17.850
You think I couldn't do anything 
without you by my side?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.520
But that was all in your head, Brother!

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:25.440
Summoning a 100-attack-point 
monster and setting one card...

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.090
You think I'll fall for that obvious trap?

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.740
Stop underestimating me!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.060
It's my turn!

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:38.700
I summon Lyrilusc — Cobalt 
Sparrow from my hand!

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:47.000
And when there's a Lyrilusc, other than 
Sapphire Swallow on my field,

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:50.030
I can Special Summon Sapphire Swallow,

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.720
along with a Level 1 Lyrilusc in my hand.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:56.000
Appear, Lyrilusc — Sapphire Swallow!

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.690
And a second Cobalt Sparrow!

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:08.910
When I successfully Special 
Summon Cobalt Sparrow,

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:12.810
I can add a third Cobalt Sparrow 
to my hand from my deck,

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:17.140
and Special Summon it with a second 
Sapphire Swallow in my hand!

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.950
Then, I overlay my three 
Level 1 Cobalt Sparrows

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.940
and two Level 2 Sapphire Swallows!

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:40.530
Birds with beautiful wings, assemble on 
the battlefield and shine in glory!

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:42.230
Xyz Summon!

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:47.990
Descend, Rank 1 Lyrilusc — 
Assembled Nightingale!

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:52.800
For each Overlay Unit Assembled 
Nightingale possesses,

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.910
its attack points increase by 100.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:02.950
In addition, it can attack you directly as 
many times as it has Overlay Units.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.930
There's no question... 
This is definitely Ruri's deck.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:10.520
And this is the strategy Ruri excels at.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.900
But they are unsuited to one 
who has fallen into darkness!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.370
Direct attack, one!

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.740
Two!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.640
Three!

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.590
What's wrong?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.180
Don't you Lancers use Action Cards?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:33.150
Four!

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.820
I guess you don't have time.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:38.690
Five!

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.480
Without you by my side, 
I can do nothing, you say?

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.800
Never say that again!

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.610
I end my turn.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:55.850
Heartless... So heartless.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.590
Beautifully heartless!

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:03.280
My Parasite Monster has torn apart 
even the bonds between siblings...

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.840
Brilliant!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.930
Listen to me, Ruri.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:13.000
I don't care who wins this duel!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.760
I just want to use the duel to bring you back.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.530
No, I will bring you back.

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.390
My turn!

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.520
I don't belong to anyone.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.650
And I am not your possession!

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:02.440
Looks like my pursuer gave up, at least...

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.940
I activate Rank-Up-Magic Raid Force!

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:11.450
I use Rise Falcon as a component to overlay!

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:19.470
Ferocious falcon, cut through fierce 
battles and flap your wings

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.530
to defeat your enemies.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.760
Rank Up Xyz Change.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:29.930
Appear, Rank 5 Raidraptor — Blaze Falcon!

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.720
I activate Blaze Falcon's effect!

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:40.940
I use one Overlay Unit to destroy all Special 
Summoned monsters on your field,

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:45.380
and to deal 500 damage to you 
for each monster destroyed!

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.860
I activate Assembled Nightingale's effect!

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.130
I use one Overlay Unit to negate battle

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:58.460
against Assembled Nightingale 
and prevent its destruction.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.670
You avoided destruction, 
but losing one Overlay Unit

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:07.130
reduces Assembled Nightingale's 
attack points by 100.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:11.880
And Blaze Falcon can attack you directly.

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.050
Open your eyes, Ruri!

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:19.720
I activate Assembled Nightingale's effect!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:25.120
I use one Overlay Unit to reduce battle 
damage to me to 0, one time!

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:31.460
Using another Overlay Unit

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:35.170
reduces Assembled Nightingale's 
attack points by another 100!

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:37.400
I now end my turn.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:39.240
My turn!

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.790
Assembled Nightingale's effect.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:48.210
It can attack directly as many 
times as it has Overlay Units.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.580
B-Brother...

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:02.890
What?

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.730
What's going on, Brother?

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:08.860
You didn't finish me off.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:13.400
Even if Academia is controlling you, 
the deck you use is the same.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:16.240
So you can't beat your brother, 
who knows that deck,

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.810
inside and out.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.710
Remember those words for later.

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:24.010
I activate Quick-Play Spell 
Lyrilusc — Bird Song!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:30.170
I can Special Summon one Level 1 monster 
from my hand, in defense position.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:33.850
I summon Fusion Parasite!

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.860
Wh-What is that?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.700
That isn't one of your monsters!

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:44.970
Save your surprise until I'm finished.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.840
When I Special Summon Fusion Parasite,

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:51.710
I can use it to Fusion Summon 
without a Polymerization card.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:54.380
What? Ruri, Fusion Summoning?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:14:00.890
I fuse Assembled Nightingale 
and Fusion Parasite!

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:05.240
Songbird who sings through the night,

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:09.130
become one with my internal voice 
and sing out more strongly!

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.600
Fusion Summon!

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:14.070
Descend, sublime and transcendent 
singer of the night!

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:18.200
Lyrilusc — Independent Nightingale!

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:26.180
Fusion Parasite becomes an equipment card for 
the monster it was used to Fusion Summon.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:31.490
And when Independent Nightingale is 
successfully Fusion Summoned,

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.660
its level increases by the

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:38.650
number of Overlay Units on the Assembled 
Nightingale used as a Fusion component.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.500
In addition, its attack points increase 
by its level times 500!

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.210
Ruri would never use Fusion Summoning.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.270
I know it now, for sure.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.610
That parasite-like monster is controlling Ruri.

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:55.740
There's no doubt.

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:57.070
Battle.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:15:01.050
I attack Blaze Falcon with 
Independent Nightingale!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:04.680
Trap card Raidraptor — Evasion!

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:08.500
I return one Raidraptor Overlay 
Unit to my hand,

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:12.420
to negate an attack against Blaze Falcon!

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.100
It isn't over yet.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.030
I activate Independent Nightingale's effect!

00:15:20.030 --> 00:15:25.380
Once per turn, I can deal its level 
times 500 as damage to you!

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:30.360
Action Spell Acceleration.

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.240
I reduce effect damage to 0.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:38.490
Surprisingly stubborn, for someone who 
said he didn't care who won or lost...

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:42.670
Clearly, as the older brother, you don't 
want to lose to your little sister.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.720
That's the kind of person you are.

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:49.900
I activate Lyrilusc — Bird Strike from my hand!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:52.700
I negate Blaze Falcon's monster effect.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:16:00.740
Now, Blaze Falcon cannot use its monster 
effect to destroy Independent Nightingale!

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.970
I now end my turn.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.470
My turn!

00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:10.450
Do you remember, Ruri?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:16.320
When you dueled Sayaka at the 
Clover Branch duel tournament?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:25.050
Winner, Clover Branch level 1, 
Sayaka Sasayama!

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.480
Little Fairy?

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.040
Is this for me?

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:42.910
Yes.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:46.620
But this is your most important card!

00:16:47.460 --> 00:16:49.680
That's why I want you to have it.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:52.320
Because you're my most important friend.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.370
Sayaka...

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.160
Ruri, don't take it!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:56.290
Brother!

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:02.870
If you're a duelist,

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:07.820
you shouldn't give your own 
cards away so casually.

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:12.720
At the time, I couldn't understand 
what Sayaka was doing.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.700
No, it was more than that.

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:18.050
After losing you, it made me even angrier.

00:17:18.560 --> 00:17:20.430
I don't want to listen to you, Brother.

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.520
Hurry up and play!

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:27.300
But meeting Yuya Sakaki and making allies 
known as the Lancers, has changed me.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:30.840
I understand now what Sayaka was doing.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:33.100
I...

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:36.200
I summon Little Fairy!

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.910
What? Little Fairy?

00:17:41.300 --> 00:17:43.140
Kaito left it with me!

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:51.130
And Sayaka likely entrusted Kaito with it.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.750
Syun, use this!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.190
I activate Little Fairy's effect!

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:03.330
I send one card from my hand to my 
graveyard, to increase its level by 1.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:06.260
That effect can be used twice per turn.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:13.130
I also activate my spell card 
Cross Xyz from my hand!

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:18.540
Using two monsters on my field 
of the same rank and level,

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.080
I can Xyz Summon.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:23.280
Xyz Summoning with rank and level?

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:29.590
I overlay Rank 5 Blaze Falcon 
and Level 5 Little Fairy!

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:34.070
Falcon whose daring is not yet seen,

00:18:34.070 --> 00:18:38.760
spread your fierce wings and 
show your hidden power!

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:41.600
Cross Xyz Summon!

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:48.260
Appear, Rank 5 Raidraptor — 
Stranger Falcon!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.860
Listen carefully, Ruri.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:54.250
It isn't just me...

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:59.100
Sayaka, Kaito, and our many allies 
are waiting for your return.

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:01.290
None of that matters to me.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.190
Stop talking nonsense!

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:06.840
In order to recover the Ruri I 
know, it seems I must do it.

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:10.490
The Ruri you know? That's just 
an illusion you created, Brother!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.480
I activate Stranger Falcon's effect!

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.510
I use one Overlay Unit

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.440
and destroy Independent Nightingale,

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:24.180
dealing its attack points as 
damage to you, Ruri!

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:28.280
That won't work.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:31.740
I send Fusion Parasite to the 
graveyard to negate the—

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:33.380
M-My hand...

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.850
I won't let you do it!

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.340
Brother...

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:54.040
Is that you, Ruri?

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.510
Brother, shoot me!

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:04.520
Raidraptor — Stranger Falcon 
attacks Ruri Kurosaki directly!

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:14.760
Ruri!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.230
Ruri, you're safe now. I'm with you.

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:22.930
Interesting... Truly interesting.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:26.640
I've gotten some extremely 
intriguing data from this!

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:27.910
I must go, at once!

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:30.650
I see there is still room for improvement.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.090
I've been looking for you, Sawatari.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.440
Oh, it's just you, Crow...

00:20:43.440 --> 00:20:45.500
Don't scare me like that.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.790
Hush! Someone's here.

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:22.940
There they are.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:24.230
The Lancers...

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:28.310
Are you the ones who've been chasing me?

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:31.200
Fine, we'll fight you.

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:32.410
Duel!

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:39.140
I, the super, ultra, hyper-strong duelist 
Shingo Sawatari, shall go first!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.080
My tur—

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:42.350
2000-point penalty for entering the battle.

00:21:44.210 --> 00:21:45.950
Give me a break!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.690
Who dares interrupt the great, super, 
ultra, hyper-strong duelist?

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:52.570
Nobody's there...

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:56.380
Are the duel disks broken?

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:57.360
What is it?

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.130
Of course they aren't!

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:00.880
Who's there? Where are you?

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.330
Show yourself!

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:50.570
All destroyed?

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:55.110
Not even the elites I hand-raised 
could surpass him?

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:58.850
Not just Tsukikage... The Academia duelists 
are being turned into cards, one by one.

00:23:59.130 --> 00:24:00.910
What is that thing?

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:04.390
Who's the third party, with 
neither us nor Academia?

00:24:04.390 --> 00:24:06.260
Watch carefully!

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:09.100
That is the ultimate Battle Beast,

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:11.430
also known as "BB"!

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:15.260
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Battle Beast.

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.380
The fun is only getting started!
